content.text:
The fault is confined to the request side of `search → rate.GetRates`, and the connection itself is healthy: network IO is unchanged and there are no network errors. I have enough evidence to write up the answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5) p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "search's outgoing rate.Rate/GetRates client spans have p50 about 1532 ms and p95 about 2813 ms during the incident."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "rate's own GetRates server spans stay fast, with p95 about 0.9 ms, so the delay is outside rate's handler."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT round(approx_quantile(epoch_ms(s.time)-epoch_ms(c.time),0.5),1) req_side_gap_p50_ms, round(approx_quantile((epoch_ms(c.time)+c.duration/1e6)-(epoch_ms(s.time)+s.duration/1e6),0.5),1) resp_side_gap_p50_ms, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON c.span_id=s.parent_span_id AND c.trace_id=s.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND s.service_name='rate'",
          "claim": "The search-to-rate gap is on the request side (about 1531 ms before rate starts); the response side is normal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, count(*) n, round(avg(value)/1e6,1) avg_mb FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric IN ('k8s.pod.network.errors','k8s.pod.network.io') AND service_name IN ('search','rate') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Network errors are zero and network IO on search and rate is at normal levels, so the connection itself is healthy."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5) p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "search's calls to geo from the same pods are unaffected, at about 0.5 ms p50, so the delay is specific to the rate path."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels') OR (service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "frontend's HTTP /hotels p95 rises to about 2828 ms, matching search's Nearby server p95 of about 2814 ms."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

